From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:44:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] GPU: VICTORY_BACK_OWN_VIEW=1: copy-backs into title
 view memory through a view of our own (hand port, off by default)

The other half of fork #1188, from the fork's a2537066 / 39731795: what
a merge made of title view memory is stored through a view of our own on
the same section (inplace::write_own), which no guard covers, so the
write does not read as the title's and the copy that wrote it does not
take its own output in again. The journal is told the page changed at
every address that shows it (watch::wrote_own, now with the other
addresses), and the writing copy notes itself current
(Shadow::put_back_own). `alt` turns it on and off every twenty seconds
for measuring.

Taken: inplace back_own / Own / write_own as they are, put_back_own
without its VICTORY_BACK_OWN_CHECK part, called in relay_merge and
card_merge_relay after put_back_quiet, as in the fork. Not taken:
JOIN_PARTS, the card meter, the frame log.

Not compiled when written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
